# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads.
#
# Without this file gcloud falls back to .gitignore, which happens to exclude the right
# things — but only by accident. Being explicit matters most for backend/vendor/: those
# are the EmoNet clones, ~270 MB of CC BY-NC-ND weights. Deployed images use the browser
# (MediaPipe, Apache-2.0) FER path, so the server-side model is neither needed nor
# something to publish in a container image. EmoNet stays a local, research-only option.

.git
.gitignore

# rebuilt inside the image
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# server-side FER: local research use only, never deployed (see docs/13)
backend/vendor/

# not needed to build or run
docs/figures/
*.log
*.md
!README.md
